IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `poca-nouns`

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, sections 337 to 339ZG (protected disclosures; authorised disclosures; form and manner; disclosures to the NCA;
-- voluntary disclosures within the regulated sector) -- LAYER 1.   Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
--
-- SHAPE.  A protection ("is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information") that the text states with its conditions
-- ("A disclosure which satisfies the following three conditions", "Where ...", "if ...") is JUST TRUE when they are met and JUST FALSE when one is not
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05: a condition stated for the protection works like "if").
-- A protection given to a class of disclosure whose conditions are not in the sentence ("An authorised disclosure", "A disclosure made in pursuance of a request")
-- is a scope limit with no "only", and stays NOTHING outside the class (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).
-- A condition ("The first condition is that ...") is a closed definition: JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE.
-- "As soon as is practicable" and "as soon as reasonably practicable" carry no number: the rules take the person's own statement that the disclosure
-- was made as soon as practicable, as a fact.  Judgments handed to a court ("reasonable excuse", "reasonable grounds") are taken as the person's stated fact.
-- To whom a disclosure is made is the noun `Person to whom a disclosure is made` of poca-nouns.l4; s 340(13) makes a person authorised by the Director General
-- of the National Crime Agency a "constable", which these rules apply.

§ `Sections 337 to 339ZG: disclosures`

§§ `s 337: protected disclosures`

-- src:487 | (2) The first condition is that the information or other matter disclosed came to the person making the disclosure (the discloser) in the course of his trade, profession, business or employment.
@ref s 337(2) (src:487)
GIVEN `the information or other matter came to the discloser in the course of his trade, profession, business or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 337(2) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `the information or other matter came to the discloser in the course of his trade, profession, business or employment`

-- src:488 | (3) The second condition is that the information or other matter—
-- src:489 | (a) causes the discloser to know or suspect, or
-- src:490 | (b) gives him reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting,
-- src:491 | that another person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 337(3) (src:488-491)
GIVEN `the information or other matter causes the discloser to know or suspect that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or other matter gives him reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 337(3) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `the information or other matter causes the discloser to know or suspect that another person is engaged in money laundering` OR `the information or other matter gives him reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting that another person is engaged in money laundering`

-- Conditions are BOOLEANs; the recipient is asked as a noun.  A recipient the text does not name ("an officer of Revenue and Customs" is not "a customs officer"
-- in the sources; "anyone else") fails the condition: the condition is a closed definition.
-- src:492 | (4) The third condition is that the disclosure is made to a constable, a customs officer or a nominated officer as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter comes to the discloser.
@ref s 337(4) (src:492)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Person to whom a disclosure is made`
      `the disclosure is made as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter comes to the discloser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 337(4) the third condition is satisfied` MEANS
        `the disclosure is made as soon as is practicable after the information or other matter comes to the discloser`
    AND (   recipient EQUALS `a constable`
         OR recipient EQUALS `a customs officer`
         OR recipient EQUALS `a nominated officer`
         OR recipient EQUALS `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`)

-- src:486 | (1) A disclosure which satisfies the following three conditions is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 337(1) (src:486)
GIVEN `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(1) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first condition is satisfied` AND `the second condition is satisfied` AND `the third condition is satisfied` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure which satisfies the following three conditions is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information" (conditions stated for a protection work like 'if' (ruling of 2026-11-05, item 1): a late disclosure, a recipient the third condition does not name, or information that did not come in the course of trade, profession, business or employment leaves the disclosure unprotected under this subsection)

-- src:493 | (4A) Where a disclosure consists of a disclosure protected under subsection (1) and a disclosure of either or both of—
-- src:494 | (a) the identity of the other person mentioned in subsection (3), and
-- src:495 | (b) the whereabouts of property forming the subject-matter of the money laundering that the discloser knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that other person to be engaged in,
-- src:496 | the disclosure of the thing mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) (as well as the disclosure protected under subsection (1)) is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 337(4A) (src:493-496)
GIVEN `the disclosure is protected under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it also discloses the identity of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it also discloses the whereabouts of property forming the subject-matter of the money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(4A) the further disclosure is not to be taken to breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is protected under subsection (1)` AND (`it also discloses the identity of the other person` OR `it also discloses the whereabouts of property forming the subject-matter of the money laundering`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure consists of a disclosure protected under subsection (1) and a disclosure of either or both of" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')

-- src:497 | (5) A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which—
-- src:498 | (a) is made to a person nominated by the discloser’s employer to receive disclosures undersection 330 or this section, and
-- src:499 | (b) is made in the course of the discloser’s employment ....
@ref s 337(5) (src:497-499)
GIVEN `it is made to a person nominated by the discloser's employer to receive disclosures under section 330 or section 337` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in the course of the discloser's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 337(5) the disclosure is a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is made to a person nominated by the discloser's employer to receive disclosures under section 330 or section 337` AND `it is made in the course of the discloser's employment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which"

§§ `s 338: authorised disclosures`

-- src:505 | (2) The first condition is that the disclosure is made before the alleged offender does the prohibited act.
@ref s 338(2) (src:505)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made before the alleged offender does the prohibited act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 338(2) the first condition is satisfied` MEANS
    `the disclosure is made before the alleged offender does the prohibited act`

-- src:506 | (2A) The second condition is that—
-- src:507 | (a) the disclosure is made while the alleged offender is doing the prohibited act,
-- src:508 | (b) he began to do the act at a time when, because he did not then know or suspect that the property constituted or represented a person's benefit from criminal conduct, the act was not a prohibited act, and
-- src:509 | (c) the disclosure is made on his own initiative and as soon as is practicable after he first knows or suspects that the property constitutes or represents a person's benefit from criminal conduct.
@ref s 338(2A) (src:506-509)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made while the alleged offender is doing the prohibited act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he began to do the act at a time when, because he did not then know or suspect that the property constituted or represented a person's benefit from criminal conduct, the act was not a prohibited act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made on his own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made as soon as is practicable after he first knows or suspects that the property constitutes or represents a person's benefit from criminal conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 338(2A) the second condition is satisfied` MEANS
        `the disclosure is made while the alleged offender is doing the prohibited act`
    AND `he began to do the act at a time when, because he did not then know or suspect that the property constituted or represented a person's benefit from criminal conduct, the act was not a prohibited act`
    AND `the disclosure is made on his own initiative`
    AND `the disclosure is made as soon as is practicable after he first knows or suspects that the property constitutes or represents a person's benefit from criminal conduct`

-- src:510 | (3) The third condition is that—
-- src:511 | (a) the disclosure is made after the alleged offender does the prohibited act,
-- src:512 | (b) he has a reasonable excuse for his failure to make the disclosure before he did the act, and
-- src:513 | (c) the disclosure is made on his own initiative and as soon as it is practicable for him to make it.
@ref s 338(3) (src:510-513)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made after the alleged offender does the prohibited act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has a reasonable excuse for his failure to make the disclosure before he did the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made on his own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made as soon as it is practicable for him to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 338(3) the third condition is satisfied` MEANS
        `the disclosure is made after the alleged offender does the prohibited act`
    AND `he has a reasonable excuse for his failure to make the disclosure before he did the act`
    AND `the disclosure is made on his own initiative`
    AND `the disclosure is made as soon as it is practicable for him to make it`

-- s 338(1)(b) is shown as dots only in the deposited text (coverage table: repealed or blank in this text).
-- src:501 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a disclosure is authorised if—
-- src:502 | (a) it is a disclosure to a constable, a customs officer or a nominated officer by the alleged offender that property is criminal property,
-- src:503 | (b) ... and
-- src:504 | (c) the first , second or third condition set out below is satisfied.
@ref s 338(1) (src:501-504)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Person to whom a disclosure is made`
      `the disclosure is made by the alleged offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is that property is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third condition is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(1) the disclosure is authorised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       (   recipient EQUALS `a constable`
                  OR recipient EQUALS `a customs officer`
                  OR recipient EQUALS `a nominated officer`
                  OR recipient EQUALS `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`)
             AND `the disclosure is made by the alleged offender`
             AND `the disclosure is that property is criminal property`
             AND (`the first condition is satisfied` OR `the second condition is satisfied` OR `the third condition is satisfied`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Part a disclosure is authorised if" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- src:514 | (4) An authorised disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 338(4) (src:514)
GIVEN `the disclosure is an authorised disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(4) the authorised disclosure is not to be taken to breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is an authorised disclosure` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is given to "An authorised disclosure"

-- src:515 | (4A) Where an authorised disclosure is made in good faith, no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person by or on whose behalf it is made.
@ref s 338(4A) (src:515)
GIVEN `the disclosure is an authorised disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(4A) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is an authorised disclosure` AND `it is made in good faith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an authorised disclosure is made in good faith" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')

-- src:516 | (5) A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which—
-- src:517 | (a) is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender’s employer to receive authorised disclosures, and
-- src:518 | (b) is made in the course of the alleged offender’s employment ....
@ref s 338(5) (src:516-518)
GIVEN `it is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender's employer to receive authorised disclosures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in the course of the alleged offender's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(5) the disclosure is a disclosure to a nominated officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is made to a person nominated by the alleged offender's employer to receive authorised disclosures` AND `it is made in the course of the alleged offender's employment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure to a nominated officer is a disclosure which"

-- src:519 | (6) References to the prohibited act are to an act mentioned in section 327(1), 328(1) or 329(1) (as the case may be).
@ref s 338(6) (src:519)
GIVEN `it is an act mentioned in section 327(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an act mentioned in section 328(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an act mentioned in section 329(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 338(6) the act is the prohibited act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an act mentioned in section 327(1)` OR `it is an act mentioned in section 328(1)` OR `it is an act mentioned in section 329(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to the prohibited act are to an act mentioned in section 327(1), 328(1) or 329(1)"

§§ `s 339: form and manner of disclosures`

-- s 339(2) (what the power to prescribe the form includes) is a rule-making power: machinery (coverage table: inert, reason 2).
-- s 339(1) names the holder of the power, which is all the text says of it; what the order prescribes is not in the sources.
-- The offence of s 339(1A) is encoded relative to a form and manner the person states have been prescribed.
DECLARE `Who prescribes the form and manner of a disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary of State`
    `someone else`

-- src:521 | (1) The Secretary of State may by order prescribe the form and manner in which a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338 must be made.
@ref s 339(1) (src:521)
GIVEN who IS A `Who prescribes the form and manner of a disclosure`
      `the disclosure is one under section 330, 331, 332 or 338` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(1) the person may by order prescribe the form and manner of the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `the Secretary of State` AND `the disclosure is one under section 330, 331, 332 or 338` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may by order prescribe the form and manner in which a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338 must be made" gives the power to the Secretary of State over those disclosures, and says nothing of anyone else or of any other disclosure (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c): a scope limit with no 'only')


-- src:522 | (1A) A person commits an offence if he makes a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338 otherwise than in the form prescribed under subsection (1) or otherwise than in the manner so prescribed.
@ref s 339(1A) (src:522)
GIVEN `he makes a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in the form prescribed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in the manner prescribed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has a reasonable excuse for making the disclosure otherwise than in the form or the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(1A) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `he makes a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he makes a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338 otherwise than" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF `the disclosure is made in the form prescribed under subsection (1)` AND `the disclosure is made in the manner prescribed under subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than in the form prescribed under subsection (1) or otherwise than in the manner so prescribed" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `he has a reasonable excuse for making the disclosure otherwise than in the form or the manner prescribed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a person does not commit an offence under subsection (1A) if he has a reasonable excuse" (s 339(1B))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:523 | (1B) But a person does not commit an offence under subsection (1A) if he has a reasonable excuse for making the disclosure otherwise than in the form prescribed under subsection (1) or (as the case may be) otherwise than in the manner so prescribed.
@ref s 339(1B) (src:523)
GIVEN `he has a reasonable excuse for making the disclosure otherwise than in the form or the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 339(1A) the person must not make a disclosure otherwise than in the prescribed form or manner unless he has a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF `he has a reasonable excuse for making the disclosure otherwise than in the form or the manner prescribed`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `make a disclosure otherwise than in the prescribed form or manner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 339(1A): a disclosure under section 330, 331, 332 or 338 was made otherwise than in the form or manner prescribed"

-- src:525 | (3) Where under subsection (2) a request is included in a form prescribed under subsection (1), the form must—
-- src:526 | (a) state that there is no obligation to comply with the request, and
-- src:527 | (b) explain the protection conferred by subsection (4) on a person who complies with the request.
@ref s 339(3) (src:525-527)
GIVEN `the prescribed form includes a request under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form states that there is no obligation to comply with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form explains the protection conferred by subsection (4) on a person who complies with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(3) the form complies with the requirements for a form that includes a request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prescribed form includes a request under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where under subsection (2) a request is included in a form prescribed under subsection (1), the form must" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `the form states that there is no obligation to comply with the request` AND `the form explains the protection conferred by subsection (4) on a person who complies with the request` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the form must (a) state that there is no obligation to comply with the request, and (b) explain the protection"

-- src:528 | (4) A disclosure made in pursuance of a request under subsection (2) is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 339(4) (src:528)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made in pursuance of a request under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(4) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is made in pursuance of a request under subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is given to "A disclosure made in pursuance of a request under subsection (2)"

-- s 339(5) and (6) are shown as dots only in the deposited text (coverage table: repealed or blank in this text).

-- src:531 | (7) Subsection (2) does not apply to a disclosure made to a nominated officer.
@ref s 339(7) (src:531)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339(7) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is made to a nominated officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "a disclosure made to a nominated officer"

§§ `s 339ZA: disclosures to the NCA`

-- s 340(13): "References to a constable include references to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency", so a disclosure to such a person is a disclosure to a constable.
-- The duty is on the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs, who has no seat in this encoding: the person meets it as what happens to a disclosure
-- he makes.  "As soon as practicable" carries no number, so the regulative rule has no WITHIN; the decision function says whether the duty applies.
-- src:533 | Where a disclosure is made under this Part to a constable or an officer of Revenue and Customs, the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs must disclose it in full to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency as soon as practicable after it has been made.
@ref s 339ZA (src:533)
GIVEN `a disclosure is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `Person to whom a disclosure is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZA the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs must disclose it in full to an authorised person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a disclosure is made under this Part` AND (recipient EQUALS `a constable` OR recipient EQUALS `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` OR recipient EQUALS `an officer of Revenue and Customs`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the text's own duty: "must disclose it in full to a person authorised ... as soon as practicable"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure is made under this Part to a constable or an officer of Revenue and Customs" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')

@ref s 339ZA (src:533)
GIVEN `a disclosure is made under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `Person to whom a disclosure is made`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 339ZA the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs must disclose the disclosure in full to an authorised person` MEANS
    IF `a disclosure is made under this Part` AND (recipient EQUALS `a constable` OR recipient EQUALS `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency` OR recipient EQUALS `an officer of Revenue and Customs`)
    THEN PARTY `the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs`
         MUST `disclose in full to a person authorised by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the constable or officer of Revenue and Customs` BECAUSE "s 339ZA: the disclosure was not disclosed in full to a person authorised by the Director General of the National Crime Agency"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 339ZB: voluntary disclosures within the regulated sector`

-- src:537 | (a) A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking,
-- src:538 | (b) the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business, and
-- src:539 | (c) the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or each of them, where the disclosure is to more than one person) is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking (whether or not of the same kind as A).
@ref s 339ZB(2) (src:537-539)
GIVEN `A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each person to whom the information is to be disclosed is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(2) condition 1 is met` MEANS
    `A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking` AND `the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business` AND `each person to whom the information is to be disclosed is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking`

-- src:541 | (a) an NCA authorised officer has requested A to make the disclosure, or
-- src:542 | (b) the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or at least one of them, where the disclosure is to more than one person) has requested A to do so.
@ref s 339ZB(3) (src:541-542)
GIVEN `an NCA authorised officer has requested A to make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one of the persons to whom the information is to be disclosed has requested A to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(3) condition 2 is met` MEANS
    `an NCA authorised officer has requested A to make the disclosure` OR `at least one of the persons to whom the information is to be disclosed has requested A to do so`

-- src:543 | (4) Condition 3 is that, before A makes the disclosure, the required notification has been made to an NCA authorised officer (see section 339ZC(3) to (5)).
@ref s 339ZB(4) (src:543)
GIVEN `before A makes the disclosure, the required notification has been made to an NCA authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(4) condition 3 is met` MEANS
    `before A makes the disclosure, the required notification has been made to an NCA authorised officer`

-- src:544 | (5) Condition 4 is that A is satisfied that the disclosure of the information will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 339ZB(5) (src:544)
GIVEN `A is satisfied that the disclosure of the information will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(5) condition 4 is met` MEANS
    `A is satisfied that the disclosure of the information will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering`

-- src:535 | (1) A person (A) may disclose information to one or more other persons if conditions 1 to 4 are met.
@ref s 339ZB(1) (src:535)
GIVEN `condition 1 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 2 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 3 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 4 is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(1) A may disclose information to one or more other persons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `condition 1 is met` AND `condition 2 is met` AND `condition 3 is met` AND `condition 4 is met` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (A) may disclose information to one or more other persons if conditions 1 to 4 are met" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))

-- src:545 | (6) A person may disclose information to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request if, and to the extent that, the person has reason to believe that A has in A's possession information that will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering.
@ref s 339ZB(6) (src:545)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reason to believe that A has in A's possession information that will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZB(6) the person may disclose information to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is made to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request` AND `the person has reason to believe that A has in A's possession information that will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may disclose information to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request if, and to the extent that" (marginal reading (a))

§§ `s 339ZC: disclosure requests and required notifications`

-- src:547 | (1) A disclosure request must—
-- src:548 | (a) state that it is made in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering,
-- src:549 | (b) identify the person (if known),
-- src:550 | (c) describe the information that is sought from A, and
-- src:551 | (d) specify the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed.
@ref s 339ZC(1) (src:547-551)
GIVEN `it states that it is made in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies the person (if known)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it describes the information that is sought from A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZC(1) the disclosure request has the content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it states that it is made in connection with a suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` AND `it identifies the person (if known)` AND `it describes the information that is sought from A` AND `it specifies the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure request must"

-- src:552 | (2) Where the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b), the request must also—
-- src:553 | (a) set out the grounds for the suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering, or
-- src:554 | (b) provide such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate for the purposes of enabling A to determine whether the information requested ought to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1).
@ref s 339ZC(2) (src:552-554)
GIVEN `the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the grounds for the suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate for the purposes of enabling A to determine whether the information requested ought to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZC(2) the disclosure request has the further content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b), the request must also" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `it sets out the grounds for the suspicion that a person is engaged in money laundering` OR `it provides such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate for the purposes of enabling A to determine whether the information requested ought to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the request must also (a) set out the grounds ... or (b) provide such other information"

-- src:555 | (3) A required notification must be made—
-- src:556 | (a) in the case of a disclosure request made by an NCA authorised officer, by the person who is to disclose information under section 339ZB(1) as a result of the request;
-- src:557 | (b) in the case of a disclosure request made by a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b), by the person who made the request.
@ref s 339ZC(3) (src:555-557)
DECLARE `Who made the disclosure request` IS ONE OF
    `an NCA authorised officer`
    `a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b)`
    `another person`

DECLARE `Who must make the required notification` IS ONE OF
    `the person who is to disclose information under section 339ZB(1) as a result of the request`
    `the person who made the request`

GIVEN requester IS A `Who made the disclosure request`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who must make the required notification`
`s 339ZC(3) who must make the required notification` MEANS
    CONSIDER requester
    WHEN `an NCA authorised officer` THEN JUST `the person who is to disclose information under section 339ZB(1) as a result of the request`
    WHEN `a person mentioned in section 339ZB(3)(b)` THEN JUST `the person who made the request`
    WHEN `another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (a) and (b) deal with the two kinds of request only

-- src:558 | (4) In a case within subsection (3)(a), the required notification must state that information is to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1).
@ref s 339ZC(4) (src:558)
GIVEN `the case is within subsection (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required notification states that information is to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZC(4) the required notification has the content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case is within subsection (3)(a)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case within subsection (3)(a), the required notification must state" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if'; 'in a case within' read as 'where')
        IF `the required notification states that information is to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the required notification must state that information is to be disclosed under section 339ZB(1)"

-- src:559 | (5) In a case within subsection (3)(b), the required notification must—
-- src:560 | (a) state that a disclosure request has been made,
-- src:561 | (b) specify the person to whom the request was made,
-- src:562 | (c) identify any person (if known) suspected of being engaged in money laundering in connection with whom the request was made, and
-- src:563 | (d) provide all such other information that the person giving the notification would be required to give if making the required disclosure for the purposes of section 330 (see in particular subsection (5)(b) and (c) of that section).
@ref s 339ZC(5) (src:559-563)
GIVEN `the case is within subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that a disclosure request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the person to whom the request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it identifies any person (if known) suspected of being engaged in money laundering in connection with whom the request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides all such other information that the person giving the notification would be required to give if making the required disclosure for the purposes of section 330` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZC(5) the required notification has the content it must have` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case is within subsection (3)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case within subsection (3)(b), the required notification must" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if'; 'in a case within' read as 'where')
        IF       `it states that a disclosure request has been made`
             AND `it specifies the person to whom the request was made`
             AND `it identifies any person (if known) suspected of being engaged in money laundering in connection with whom the request was made`
             AND `it provides all such other information that the person giving the notification would be required to give if making the required disclosure for the purposes of section 330`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the required notification must (a) state ... (b) specify ... (c) identify ... and (d) provide"

§§ `s 339ZD: effect of a required notification or joint report on the required disclosure`

-- s 339ZD(1) says when the section applies (a question arises in proceedings whether the required disclosure under s 330(4) or 331(4) has been made by A, B or C):
-- the question is an input of the rules of (2) and (3) below.

-- src:578 | (5) The requirements as to content are that the report must—
-- src:579 | (a) explain the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person mentioned in subsection (4)(c) is engaged in money laundering,
-- src:580 | (b) identify the person (if known),
-- src:581 | (c) set out the grounds for the suspicion, and
-- src:582 | (d) provide any other information relevant to the matter.
@ref s 339ZD(5) (src:578-582)
GIVEN `the report explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person mentioned in subsection (4)(c) is engaged in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report identifies the person (if known)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report sets out the grounds for the suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report provides any other information relevant to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(5) the report satisfies the requirements as to content` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `the report explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person mentioned in subsection (4)(c) is engaged in money laundering`
             AND `the report identifies the person (if known)`
             AND `the report sets out the grounds for the suspicion`
             AND `the report provides any other information relevant to the matter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements as to content are that the report must"

-- src:583 | (6) The applicable period is—
-- src:584 | (a) in a case where the disclosure under section 339ZB was made as a result of a disclosure request from an NCA authorised officer by virtue of subsection (3)(a) of that section, whatever period may be specified by the officer when making the request;
-- src:585 | (b) in a case where the disclosure was made as a result of a disclosure request from another person by virtue of subsection (3)(b) of that section, the period of 84 days beginning with the day on which a required notification is made in connection with the request.
@ref s 339ZD(6) (src:583-585)
GIVEN `the disclosure request was made by an NCA authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the period specified by the officer when making the request, if he specified one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which a required notification is made in connection with the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 339ZD(6) the last day of the applicable period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure request was made by an NCA authorised officer` THEN `the last day of the period specified by the officer when making the request, if he specified one` -- NOTHING when he specified none: the text says only "whatever period may be specified by the officer"
        OTHERWISE JUST ((`the day on which a required notification is made in connection with the request`) PLUS 83) -- 84 days beginning with the day of the notification

-- src:573 | (4) A joint disclosure report is a report to an NCA authorised officer that—
-- src:574 | (a) is made jointly by A and B (whether or not also jointly with other persons to whom A discloses information under section 339ZB(1)),
-- src:575 | (b) satisfies the requirements as to content mentioned in subsection (5),
-- src:576 | (c) is prepared after the making of a disclosure by A to B under section 339ZB(1) in connection with a suspicion of a person's engagement in money laundering, and
-- src:577 | (d) is sent to the NCA authorised officer before the end of the applicable period.
@ref s 339ZD(4) (src:573-577)
GIVEN `the report is made jointly by A and B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report satisfies the requirements as to content mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is prepared after the making of a disclosure by A to B under section 339ZB(1) in connection with a suspicion of a person's engagement in money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the report is sent to the NCA authorised officer` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the applicable period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(4) the report is a joint disclosure report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `the report is made jointly by A and B`
             AND `the report satisfies the requirements as to content mentioned in subsection (5)`
             AND `the report is prepared after the making of a disclosure by A to B under section 339ZB(1) in connection with a suspicion of a person's engagement in money laundering`
             AND `the day the report is sent to the NCA authorised officer` AT MOST `the last day of the applicable period`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A joint disclosure report is a report to an NCA authorised officer that"

-- src:569 | (2) The making of a required notification in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement to make the required disclosure on the part of A, B and C.
-- src:570 | This is subject to section 339ZE(1) to (8).
@ref s 339ZD(2) (src:569-570)
GIVEN `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made for the purposes of section 330(4) or 331(4) by A, B or C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required notification is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(2) the required notification is treated as satisfying the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made for the purposes of section 330(4) or 331(4) by A, B or C` AND `the required notification is made in good faith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is given to "The making of a required notification in good faith" in the proceedings described in subsection (1)

-- src:571 | (3) The making of a joint disclosure report in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement to make the required disclosure on the part of the persons who jointly make the report.
-- src:572 | This is subject to section 339ZE(10).
@ref s 339ZD(3) (src:571-572)
GIVEN `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made for the purposes of section 330(4) or 331(4) by A, B or C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is a joint disclosure report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(3) the joint disclosure report is treated as satisfying the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made for the purposes of section 330(4) or 331(4) by A, B or C` AND `the report is a joint disclosure report` AND `the report is made in good faith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is given to "The making of a joint disclosure report in good faith"

-- src:586 | (7) A joint disclosure report must be—
-- src:587 | (a) approved by the nominated officer of each person that jointly makes the report, and
-- src:588 | (b) signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person.
-- src:589 | If there is no nominated officer the report must be approved and signed by another senior officer.
@ref s 339ZD(7) (src:586-589)
GIVEN `each person that jointly makes the report has a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is approved by the nominated officer of each such person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is approved and signed by another senior officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(7) the joint disclosure report is approved and signed as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `each person that jointly makes the report has a nominated officer` AND `the report is approved by the nominated officer of each such person` AND `the report is signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `each person that jointly makes the report has a nominated officer`) AND `the report is approved and signed by another senior officer` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A joint disclosure report must be (a) approved by the nominated officer ... and (b) signed by the nominated officer ... If there is no nominated officer the report must be approved and signed by another senior officer"

-- src:590 | (8) References in this section to A, B or C include—
-- src:591 | (a) a nominated officer acting on behalf of A, B or C, and
-- src:592 | (b) any other person who is an employee, officer or partner of A, B or C.
@ref s 339ZD(8) (src:590-592)
GIVEN `the person is a nominated officer acting on behalf of A, B or C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee, officer or partner of A, B or C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZD(8) the person is within the references to A, B or C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a nominated officer acting on behalf of A, B or C` OR `the person is an employee, officer or partner of A, B or C` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to A, B or C include"

§§ `s 339ZE: limits on s 339ZD(2) and (3)`

-- src:594 | (1) Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where the required notification is made by A (notification made as a result of disclosure request received from NCA authorised officer).
-- src:595 | (2) Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of A, B or C only so far as relating to—
-- src:596 | (a) the suspicion in connection with which the required notification is made, and
-- src:597 | (b) matters known, suspected or believed as a result of the making of the disclosure request concerned.
@ref s 339ZE(2) (src:594-597)
GIVEN `the required notification is made by A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the required notification is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed as a result of the making of the disclosure request concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(2) section 339ZD(2) has effect on the requirement in the case of A, B or C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the required notification is made by A` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) and (3) apply in a case where the required notification is made by A" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the required notification is made` OR `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed as a result of the making of the disclosure request concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of A, B or C only so far as relating to"

-- src:598 | (3) Accordingly, section 339ZD(2) does not remove any requirement to make the required disclosure in relation to anything known, suspected or believed that does not result only from the making of the disclosure request.
@ref s 339ZE(3) (src:598)
GIVEN `the required notification is made by A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing known, suspected or believed does not result only from the making of the disclosure request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(3) section 339ZD(2) removes the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the required notification is made by A` AND `the thing known, suspected or believed does not result only from the making of the disclosure request` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 339ZD(2) does not remove any requirement to make the required disclosure in relation to anything known, suspected or believed that does not result only from the making of the disclosure request"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the case in which A makes the notification and the thing known does not result only from the request

-- src:600 | (5) Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of A or C only so far as relating to—
-- src:601 | (a) the suspicion in connection with which the notification by B is made, and
-- src:602 | (b) matters known, suspected or believed by A or C as a result of the making of that notification.
@ref s 339ZE(5) (src:600-602)
GIVEN `the required notification is made by B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the notification by B is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed by A or C as a result of the making of that notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(5) section 339ZD(2) has effect on the requirement in the case of A or C` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the required notification is made by B` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (5) to (7) apply in a case where the required notification is made by B" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the notification by B is made` OR `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed by A or C as a result of the making of that notification` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of A or C only so far as relating to"

-- src:603 | (6) Accordingly, section 339ZD(2) does not remove any requirement to make the required disclosure in relation to anything known, suspected or believed that does not result only from the making of the notification.
@ref s 339ZE(6) (src:603)
GIVEN `the required notification is made by B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing known, suspected or believed does not result only from the making of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(6) section 339ZD(2) removes the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the required notification is made by B` AND `the thing known, suspected or believed does not result only from the making of the notification` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 339ZD(2) does not remove any requirement to make the required disclosure in relation to anything known, suspected or believed that does not result only from the making of the notification"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the case in which B makes the notification and the thing known does not result only from it

-- src:604 | (7) Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of B only so far as relating to—
-- src:605 | (a) the suspicion in connection with which the notification is made, and
-- src:606 | (b) matters known, suspected or believed by B at the time of the making of the notification.
@ref s 339ZE(7) (src:604-606)
GIVEN `the required notification is made by B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the notification is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed by B at the time of the making of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(7) section 339ZD(2) has effect on the requirement in the case of B` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the required notification is made by B` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (5) to (7) apply in a case where the required notification is made by B" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the notification is made` OR `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed by B at the time of the making of the notification` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 339ZD(2) has effect in the case of B only so far as relating to"

-- src:607 | (8) If a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period (whether the required notification was made by A or B), section 339ZD(2)—
-- src:608 | (a) has effect only so far as relating to any requirement to make the required disclosure that would have otherwise arisen within that period, and
-- src:609 | (b) does not remove a requirement to make the required disclosure so far as arising after the end of that period on the part of any person in respect of matters that may become known, suspected or believed by the person after the time when the required notification was made.
@ref s 339ZE(8) (src:607-609)
GIVEN `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement would have otherwise arisen within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(8) section 339ZD(2) has effect on the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words, the text's no)
        IF `the requirement would have otherwise arisen within that period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) has effect only so far as relating to any requirement to make the required disclosure that would have otherwise arisen within that period, and (b) does not remove a requirement to make the required disclosure so far as arising after the end of that period"

-- s 339ZE(1), (4) and the lead-in of (2), (3) fix which of the rules above applies to which notification (A or B): they are inputs of those rules.
-- s 339ZE(11) ("Terms used in this section have the same meanings as in section 339ZD") is a cross-reference that creates no rule (coverage table: inert, reason 1).

-- src:610 | (9) If a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period, the person who made the required notification must notify an NCA authorised officer that a report is not being made as soon as reasonably practicable after the period ends.
@ref s 339ZE(9) (src:610)
GIVEN `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(9) the person who made the required notification must notify an NCA authorised officer that a report is not being made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period` THEN JUST TRUE -- the text's own duty: "must notify an NCA authorised officer that a report is not being made as soon as reasonably practicable after the period ends"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words, the text's no)

@ref s 339ZE(9) (src:610)
GIVEN `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 339ZE(9) the person who made the required notification must notify an NCA authorised officer that a report is not being made` MEANS
    IF `a joint disclosure report is not made before the end of the applicable period`
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         MUST `notify an NCA authorised officer that a joint disclosure report is not being made`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 339ZE(9): an NCA authorised officer was not notified that a joint disclosure report is not being made"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:611 | (10) Section 339ZD(3) has effect only so far as relating to—
-- src:612 | (a) the suspicion in connection with which the report is made, and
-- src:613 | (b) matters known, suspected or believed at the time of the making of the report.
@ref s 339ZE(10) (src:611-613)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the report is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed at the time of the making of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZE(10) section 339ZD(3) has effect on the requirement to make the required disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement relates to the suspicion in connection with which the report is made` OR `the requirement relates to matters known, suspected or believed at the time of the making of the report` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 339ZD(3) has effect only so far as relating to"

§§ `s 339ZF: supplementary`

-- src:616 | (1) A relevant disclosure made in good faith does not breach—
-- src:617 | (a) an obligation of confidence owed by the person making the disclosure, or
-- src:618 | (b) any other restriction on the disclosure of information,
-- src:619 | however imposed.
@ref s 339ZF(1) (src:616-619)
GIVEN `the disclosure is a relevant disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZF(1) the relevant disclosure does not breach an obligation of confidence or another restriction on disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is a relevant disclosure` AND `it is made in good faith` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is given to "A relevant disclosure made in good faith"

-- src:620 | (2) But a relevant disclosure may not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency unless that agency consents to the disclosure.
@ref s 339ZF(2) (src:620)
GIVEN `the relevant disclosure includes information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that agency consents to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZF(2) the relevant disclosure may not include the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the relevant disclosure includes information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition speaks only of "information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency"
        IF `that agency consents to the disclosure` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency unless that agency consents to the disclosure"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- the text's own prohibition: "a relevant disclosure may not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency"

@ref s 339ZF(2) (src:620)
GIVEN `that agency consents to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 339ZF(2) a relevant disclosure must not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency unless it consents` MEANS
    IF `that agency consents to the disclosure`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `include in a relevant disclosure information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 339ZF(2): a relevant disclosure included information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency that had not consented"

-- src:622 | (a) a relevant disclosure by the undertaking must be made by the nominated officer on behalf of the undertaking, and
@ref s 339ZF(3)(a) (src:622)
GIVEN `a person is acting on behalf of the undertaking as a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is a relevant disclosure by the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by the nominated officer on behalf of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339ZF(3)(a) the relevant disclosure by the undertaking is made as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a person is acting on behalf of the undertaking as a nominated officer` AND `the disclosure is a relevant disclosure by the undertaking`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where a person is acting on behalf of another" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        IF `it is made by the nominated officer on behalf of the undertaking` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant disclosure by the undertaking must be made by the nominated officer on behalf of the undertaking"

